# Subscope-call — declared subscope lowering (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3)

A declared subscope: the caller delegates a computation to a callee
instance and reads one output back over the synthesised back-link. The
plugin lowers the collapsed `EScopeCall` to one object creation (the args
become member initialisations on the callee inputs, plus the
`verbindendeRol` back-link) and the output read to a navigated
`AttribuutRef`. Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  input aftrek content integer
  output uitkomst content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition uitkomst equals grondslag - aftrek

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslag content integer
  input aftrek content integer
  kamer scope Kamer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition kamer.grondslag equals grondslag
  definition kamer.aftrek equals aftrek
  definition heffing equals kamer.uitkomst
```
